1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,820
What if your phone battery lasted 100 years?

2
00:00:03,260 --> 00:00:04,700
You'd never charge it again.

3
00:00:05,160 --> 00:00:07,800
And you'd probably still replace the phone in a few years.

4
00:00:08,300 --> 00:00:08,560
Why?

5
00:00:09,360 --> 00:00:10,500
First, the dream.

6
00:00:11,120 --> 00:00:11,900
No chargers.

7
00:00:12,220 --> 00:00:13,700
No 1% panic.

8
00:00:14,020 --> 00:00:16,300
No fighting over the one plug at the airport.

9
00:00:16,960 --> 00:00:17,580
Here's the catch.

10
00:00:18,100 --> 00:00:20,700
A battery that lasts this long already exists.

11
00:00:21,260 --> 00:00:25,580
A company in China built a nuclear battery it says runs for 50 years.

12
00:00:25,580 --> 00:00:28,260
But it makes about 100 microwatts.

13
00:00:28,700 --> 00:00:31,820
Your phone needs tens of thousands of times more than that.

14
00:00:32,140 --> 00:00:33,580
It couldn't even light your screen.

15
00:00:34,160 --> 00:00:39,020
And even if it worked, your phone would get slow and outdated long before the battery died.

16
00:00:40,220 --> 00:00:41,340
Now the dark part.

17
00:00:41,800 --> 00:00:43,700
Your phone would outlive you.

18
00:00:44,140 --> 00:00:46,520
A hundred years from now, it's still buzzing.

19
00:00:47,400 --> 00:00:47,760
Spam call.

20
00:00:48,300 --> 00:00:49,760
"Your car's extended warranty."

21
00:00:50,620 --> 00:00:53,640
Send this to the friend whose phone is always on 2%.

22
00:00:54,340 --> 00:00:55,360
Subscribe now.

23
00:00:55,740 --> 00:00:59,020
Your battery won't last 100 years, but this channel will.
